meta {
  name: Generate Material
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/temarios/{{temarioId}}/generar-material
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "piezas": ["teoria"],
    "modelo": "flash"
  }
}

docs {
  Selective generation — every listed piece is (re)generated. Every call is a real,
  billed OpenAI request and counts against the daily generation quota (PlanLimitService).

  piezas: any of estructura, teoria, evaluacion, diapositivas.
    - evaluacion requires teoria to already exist (or to be requested in the same call) —
      exams are generated from the theory text, not the raw syllabus.
    - diapositivas requires PlanUsuario#permiteDiapositivas (Pro).
  modelo: flash (Tutor, gpt-4.1-mini) or pro (Catedrático, o4-mini reasoning, Pro-only via
    PlanUsuario#permiteModeloPro).

  Optional per-tier overrides, each validated against the selected tier's [min, max]:
  numeroParrafos, numeroPreguntas, numeroDiapositivas, numeroModulos.

  Example requesting a full exam grounded in fresh theory in one call:
    {
      "piezas": ["teoria", "evaluacion"],
      "modelo": "flash",
      "numeroParrafos": 8,
      "numeroPreguntas": 5
    }
}
